    "headline": "Jorge Pérez Gallego, astrophysicist: ‘A total eclipse creates an energy similar to a big concert, to the feeling of celebrating a goal’",
    "summary": "For the Spaniard who directs communications at the U.S. National Solar Observatory, the unique sensations produced by the astronomical phenomenon go beyond what science can explain",
    "publisher": "Rally News",
    "url": "https://rally.news/categories/ai/?article=Jorge%2BP%C3%A9rez%2BGallego%2C%2Bastrophysicist%3A%2B%E2%80%98A%2Btotal%2Beclipse%2Bcreates%2Ban%2Benergy%2Bsimilar%2Bto%2Ba%2Bbig%2Bconcert%2C%2Bto%2Bthe%2Bfeeling%2Bof%2Bcelebrating%2Ba%2Bgoal%E2%80%99"
  },
  "researchBrief": "The story focuses on the unique experience of a total solar eclipse, as described by astrophysicist Jorge Pérez Gallego. The key points are corroborated by multiple sources, including EL PAÍS and WorldPressa. Pérez Gallego emphasizes the importance of being in the path of totality to fully experience the eclipse, comparing the energy and emotions to those of a big concert or celebrating a goal. The difference between a 99.9% eclipse and a total eclipse is highlighted, with the latter being a once-in-a-lifetime event that can inspire awe and curiosity. The sources agree on the rarity and significance of total eclipses, with Pérez Gallego noting that people will remember where they were and who they were with during the eclipse, similar to how we remember significant historical events. The story does not include specific numbers or statistics that need to be verified, focusing instead on the qualitative experience of the eclipse.",
